;; Budgets for kondo suppressions: inline `:clj-kondo/ignore` forms per linter (:ignore-counts), and
;; config-level waivers in .clj-kondo/config.edn (:config-counts -- :off switches and :exclude entries).
;; :discouraged-var-counts / :discouraged-namespace-counts budget those two linters per symbol instead
;; of per linter -- keyed by the symbol's own namespace/name, not the linter (`ee.` marks an enterprise
;; namespace, so it can't collide with its OSS counterpart of the same shape).
;; Each :ignore-counts value is a non-negative integer budget, or :unlimited for no ceiling; the two
;; per-symbol fields and :config-counts are always a plain non-negative integer.
;; Checks fail when a count exceeds its numeric budget; unused budget is allowed.
;; Any ignore outside :comment-exempt needs an explanatory comment directly above or trailing on its line;
;; this is a per-linter policy, so it stays keyed by the plain linter name even for the two split above.
;; `./bin/mage kondo-ratchets-shrink` lowers budgets unless `--seed` explicitly adds or raises one; a bare
;; `--seed :discouraged-var`/`:discouraged-namespace` seeds every symbol configured under it at once.
;; The workflow runs it on master, so feature branches do not need to record reductions.
;; Raising or adding a budget (`--seed` for inline ignores, a manual edit otherwise) or widening the
;; exemptions must be explained in the PR.
;; :all is the vector-less ignore form, which suppresses every linter on the next form.
